@stuartwdouglas Hi Stuart, what do you think, is `@Observes` needed ? Can we use ThreadLocal ?
I can try different options by re-enabling the test, the problem is it works for myself and Georgios when it is run locally :-)
 
CC @gsmet @geoand

@stuartwdouglas I think [this test](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/6610) is failing (in CI only, not in the local build) because
[this code branch is executing](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/extensions/oidc/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/runtime/OidcJsonWebTokenProducer.java#L61) while instead [this branch](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/extensions/oidc/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/runtime/OidcJsonWebTokenProducer.java#L57) is always expected to run when the access token is injected, which means to me that [this producer code](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/extensions/oidc/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/runtime/OidcJsonWebTokenProducer.java#L38) which is used to inject `Principal`is run before [this code is run](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/blob/master/extensions/oidc/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/runtime/OidcIdentityProvider.java#L74).
What do you think ?
